pg", "page": "11", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/11"}, {"image": "/13309/13309_ms1490_2_22_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/12"}, {"image": "/13309/13309_ms1490_2_22_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/13"}, {"image": "/13309/13309_ms1490_2_22_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/14"}, {"image": "/13309/13309_ms1490_2_22_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/15"}, {"image": "/13309/13309_ms1490_2_22_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "subscriptions-for-willard-richards-2-august-1843-12-march-1844", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD13", "documentSeriesTitle": "Subscriptions for Willard Richards, 2 August 1843–12 March 1844", "editorialPageNumber": "3", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54004945/54004945-0003.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> live by his liberality,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11483189157003012907\"><a href=\"#11483189157003012907\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans3\"><span id=\"documenttrans3\">3</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 32:8.</p><hr></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17912742416507894495\"><a href=\"#17912742416507894495\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> August 2<span class=\"underscore\">d</span> 1843.—</div> <span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X83480\">Names.</td> <td xml:id=\"X83481\">Materials, Labor &amp;c.</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83482\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8428678623836926349\"><a href=\"#8428678623836926349\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; JS begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\">Joseph Smith</span></td><td xml:id=\"X83484\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">one City lot</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5656334260244848071\"><a href=\"#5656334260244848071\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This presumably referred to a parcel of property located on block 103, lot 2, of the <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a> city plat where <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Richards</a> eventually constructed his home. The <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">church</a> owned the land in early 1843. In July of that year, a county sheriff transferred the property to a Mr. Hamilton when the church apparently failed to pay taxes on it; JS insisted that he had paid taxes on the property. In September 1843, JS discussed the matter with Hamilton. The issue was presumably resolved by 3 March 1845, when the property was deeded to <a href=\"/person/jennetta-richards-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jennetta Richards Richards</a> by church trustees <a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> and <a href=\"/person/george-miller\" class=\"referenceInPop\">George Miller</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1841-december-1842/19\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1841-december-1842\" poptitle=\" 2\nMarch 1842 • Wednesday\">JS, Journal, 2 Mar. 1842</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842/7\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842\" poptitle=\"2 March 1842 • WednesdaySee 2 Mar. 1842 entry in JS\n History, vol. C-1, p. 1286.\">Historian’s Office, JS History, Draft Notes, 2–3 Mar. 1842, 5</a>; Clayton, Journal, 1 Aug. 1843; <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844/91\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844\" poptitle=\"5 September 1843 • Tuesday\">JS, Journal, 5 Sept. 1843</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844/1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844\" poptitle=\"History, 1838–1856, volume E-1 [1 July 1843–30 April 1844]\">JS History, vol. E-1, 1714</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/nauvoo-registry-of-deeds-deed-record-book-b-1843-1846/297\" class=\"externalLink\">Nauvoo Registry of Deeds, Record of Deeds, bk. B, p. 287</a>.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Clayton, William. Journals, 1842–1845. CHL.</p></div></div></div></aside></td></tr><tr><td xml:id=\"X83486\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11924921500381645219\"><a href=\"#11924921500381645219\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1139959529997681658\"><a href=\"#1139959529997681658\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x112055\" person=\"x112055\" title=\"Jacob Peart\">Jacob Peart</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Peart, Jacob\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/jacob-peart\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside>. Said</td> <td xml:id=\"X83488\">2 cords of stone—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16781067464879880179\"><a href=\"#16781067464879880179\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A cord consisted of thirty-two cubic feet of stone. (Gillette, <span class=\"title\">Rock Excavation,</span> 11.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Gillette, Halbert Powers. <span class=\"title\">Rock Excavation: Methods and Cost.</span> New York: M. C. Clark, 1904.</p></div></div></div></aside> Paid</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83490\"> <table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9773467956258792053\"><a href=\"#9773467956258792053\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x54663\" person=\"x54663\" title=\"John Sanders\">John Sanders</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Sanders, John\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/john-sanders\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside>)</td> <td> </td></tr> <tr> <td>&amp;)</td> <td>said</td> </tr> <tr> <td><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9635987943378957042\"><a href=\"#9635987943378957042\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4666\" person=\"x4666\" title=\"Peter Maughan\">Peter Maughan</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Maughan, Peter\"><p>7 May 1811–24 Apr. 1871. Farmer, miner, stonemason. Born in Breconside, Farlam, Cumberland, England. Son of William Maughan and Martha Wilson. Married first Ruth Harrison, 1 Oct. 1831, in Alston, Cumberland. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/peter-maughan\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside>)</td> <td> </td></tr> </tbody></table> </td> <td xml:id=\"X83491\"> <table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td>dig and stone)</td> <td rowspan=\"2\" colspan=\"1\" valign=\"middle\">Paid.—</td> </tr> <tr> <td> a well, 15 days)</td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83492\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10788338253192897988\"><a href=\"#10788338253192897988\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans4\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscribers begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"554221754015521422\"><a href=\"#554221754015521422\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per137\" person=\"per137\" title=\"Robert D. Foster\">Robert D. Foster</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Foster, Robert D.\"><p>14 Mar. 1811–1 Feb. 1878. Justice of the peace, physician, land speculator. Born in Braunston, Northamptonshire, England. Son of John Foster and Jane Knibb. Married Sarah Phinney, 18 July 1837, at Medina Co., Ohio. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/robert-d-foster\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83494\">fifty dollars in Labor &amp; material</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83495\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16824649751248255380\"><a href=\"#16824649751248255380\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per617\" person=\"per617\" title=\"Rufus Beach\">Rufus Beach</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Beach, Rufus\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/rufus-beach\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83496\">box Glass—</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83497\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3498875314728738843\"><a href=\"#3498875314728738843\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8314994425060648252\"><a href=\"#8314994425060648252\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1025\" person=\"per1025\" title=\"Abel Lamb\">Abel Lamb</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Lamb, Abel\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/abel-lamb\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83499\">two dollars, cooper </td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83500\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6111858885259687374\"><a href=\"#6111858885259687374\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans6\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscribers begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16204031198212291919\"><a href=\"#16204031198212291919\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per521\" person=\"per521\" title=\"William Henry Harrison Sagers\">Harrison, Sagers</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Sagers, William Henry Harrison\"><p>3 May 1814/1815–19 June 1886. Painter, farmer. Born in LeRoy, Genessee Co., New York. Son of John Sagers and Amy Sweet. Moved to Elk Creek Township, Erie Co., Pennsylvania, by 1830. Baptized into Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, 27 Jan. 1833. ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/william-henry-harrison-sagers\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83502\">Brick 5.00</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83503\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12175674579707413340\"><a href=\"#12175674579707413340\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1420\" person=\"per1420\" title=\"R. T. Madison\">Robert Madison</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Madison, R. T.\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/r-t-madison\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83504\">20</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83505\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9933118989696344000\"><a href=\"#9933118989696344000\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x112498\" person=\"x112498\" title=\"William Cook\">William Cook</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Cook, William\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/william-cook\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83506\">Brick 500</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83507\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6257965285608201334\"><a href=\"#6257965285608201334\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x115548\" person=\"x115548\" title=\"James Leach\">James Leach</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Leach, James\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/james-leach\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83508\">300</td> </tr> </tbody></table> <div class=\"noindent wasptag\"> [p. 3]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> live by his liberality,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8715821196118587750\"><a href=\"#8715821196118587750\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans3\"><span id=\"documenttrans3\">3</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 32:8.</p><hr></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5025794958911727429\"><a href=\"#5025794958911727429\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> August 2<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">d</span></span> 1843.—</div> <span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X83480\">Names.</td> <td xml:id=\"X83481\">Materials, Labor &amp;<span class=\"superscript\">c.</span></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83482\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4652967408952752849\"><a href=\"#4652967408952752849\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; JS begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\">Joseph Smith</span></td><td xml:id=\"X83484\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">one City lot</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6065566495772753075\"><a href=\"#6065566495772753075\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This presumably referred to a parcel of property located on block 103, lot 2, of the <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a> city plat where <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Richards</a> eventually constructed his home. The <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">church</a> owned the land in early 1843. In July of that year, a county sheriff transferred the property to a Mr. Hamilton when the church apparently failed to pay taxes on it; JS insisted that he had paid taxes on the property. In September 1843, JS discussed the matter with Hamilton. The issue was presumably resolved by 3 March 1845, when the property was deeded to <a href=\"/person/jennetta-richards-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jennetta Richards Richards</a> by church trustees <a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> and <a href=\"/person/george-miller\" class=\"referenceInPop\">George Miller</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1841-december-1842/19\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1841-december-1842\" poptitle=\" 2\nMarch 1842 • Wednesday\">JS, Journal, 2 Mar. 1842</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842/7\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842\" poptitle=\"2 March 1842 • WednesdaySee 2 Mar. 1842 entry in JS\n History, vol. C-1, p. 1286.\">Historian’s Office, JS History, Draft Notes, 2–3 Mar. 1842, 5</a>; Clayton, Journal, 1 Aug. 1843; <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844/91\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844\" poptitle=\"5 September 1843 • Tuesday\">JS, Journal, 5 Sept. 1843</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844/1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844\" poptitle=\"History, 1838–1856, volume E-1 [1 July 1843–30 April 1844]\">JS History, vol. E-1, 1714</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/nauvoo-registry-of-deeds-deed-record-book-b-1843-1846/297\" class=\"externalLink\">Nauvoo Registry of Deeds, Record of Deeds, bk. B, p. 287</a>.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Clayton, William. Journals, 1842–1845. CHL.</p></div></div></div></aside></td></tr><tr><td xml:id=\"X83486\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10417568544306744739\"><a href=\"#10417568544306744739\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6010339261806721083\"><a href=\"#6010339261806721083\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x112055\" person=\"x112055\" title=\"Jacob Peart\">Jacob Peart</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Peart, Jacob\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/jacob-peart\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside>. Said</td> <td xml:id=\"X83488\">2 cords of stone—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6040184749055436078\"><a href=\"#6040184749055436078\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A cord consisted of thirty-two cubic feet of stone. (Gillette, <span class=\"title\">Rock Excavation,</span> 11.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Gillette, Halbert Powers. <span class=\"title\">Rock Excavation: Methods and Cost.</span> New York: M. C. Clark, 1904.</p></div></div></div></aside> &lt;​Paid​&gt;</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83490\"> <table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16474067092506897824\"><a href=\"#16474067092506897824\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x54663\" person=\"x54663\" title=\"John Sanders\">John Sanders</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Sanders, John\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/john-sanders\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside>)</td> <td> </td></tr> <tr> <td>&amp;)</td> <td>said</td> </tr> <tr> <td><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5552845284193864410\"><a href=\"#5552845284193864410\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4666\" person=\"x4666\" title=\"Peter Maughan\">Peter Maughan</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Maughan, Peter\"><p>7 May 1811–24 Apr. 1871. Farmer, miner, stonemason. Born in Breconside, Farlam, Cumberland, England. Son of William Maughan and Martha Wilson. Marrie