 href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a> city plat where <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Richards</a> eventually constructed his home. The <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">church</a> owned the land in early 1843. In July of that year, a county sheriff transferred the property to a Mr. Hamilton when the church apparently failed to pay taxes on it; JS insisted that he had paid taxes on the property. In September 1843, JS discussed the matter with Hamilton. The issue was presumably resolved by 3 March 1845, when the property was deeded to <a href=\"/person/jennetta-richards-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jennetta Richards Richards</a> by church trustees <a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> and <a href=\"/person/george-miller\" class=\"referenceInPop\">George Miller</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1841-december-1842/19\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1841-december-1842\" poptitle=\" 2\nMarch 1842 • Wednesday\">JS, Journal, 2 Mar. 1842</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842/7\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-draft-1-january-30-june-1842\" poptitle=\"2 March 1842 • WednesdaySee 2 Mar. 1842 entry in JS\n History, vol. C-1, p. 1286.\">Historian’s Office, JS History, Draft Notes, 2–3 Mar. 1842, 5</a>; Clayton, Journal, 1 Aug. 1843; <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844/91\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-december-1842-june-1844-book-3-15-july-1843-29-february-1844\" poptitle=\"5 September 1843 • Tuesday\">JS, Journal, 5 Sept. 1843</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844/1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/history-1838-1856-volume-e-1-1-july-1843-30-april-1844